{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mass.SelfMutualPartition"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.selfLinking_fixed_writhe_moved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.selfLinking_fixed_writhe_moved","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L195-L201","doc":"**The two facts side by side** — the falsifiable statement of §2. Under one and the same\ninflexional move the Călugăreanu self-linking is fixed while the writhe is not, so the two candidate\nself-energies disagree about whether the §1 gate holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.selfEnergy_not_invariant_of_writhe_valued","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.selfEnergy_not_invariant_of_writhe_valued","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L187-L193","doc":"**A self-energy read off the writhe alone can fail the gate.** For a faithful reading of the\nself-crossing count, an inflexional (type-I) move strictly changes the self-energy, so\n`selfDefect ≠ 0` and `binding = −mutual` fails. Concretely over `ℝ` with a single created\nself-crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.selfEnergy_invariant_of_factorsThroughSelfLinking","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.selfEnergy_invariant_of_factorsThroughSelfLinking","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L181-L185","doc":"**A self-energy that factors through the Călugăreanu self-linking passes the gate**: assembly\nmay reorganise writhe into twist, and the energy does not move. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.writhe_inflexionMove_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.writhe_inflexionMove_ne","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L169-L174","doc":"**The writhe alone is not** — it moves by exactly `d`. So a quantity read off the self-crossing\ncount is changed by a type-I move, which is what an ambient isotopy typically performs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.selfLinking_inflexionMove","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.selfLinking_inflexionMove","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L163-L167","doc":"**The self-linking is invariant under the inflexional exchange** — Călugăreanu's point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.inflexionMove","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.inflexionMove","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L158-L161","doc":"**The inflexional exchange.** Passing through an inflexion point shifts the writhe by `d` and\nthe twist by `−d` (Moffatt & Ricca §1: the two \"are discontinuous by equal and opposite amounts …\nso that the sum does vary continuously\"). A type-I Reidemeister move is the `d = ±1` case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.selfLinking","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.selfLinking","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L154-L156","doc":"**Călugăreanu–White–Pohl self-linking** `SL = Wr + Tw` — the combination that is the isotopy\ninvariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.Framed.twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.Framed.twist","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L150-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.Framed.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.Framed.writhe","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L149-L149","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.Framed.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.Framed.mk","kind":"ctor","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L148-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.Framed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.Framed","kind":"structure","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L147-L150","doc":"A framed (ribbon) component, carried by its writhe and its normalised total twist. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.gate_has_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.gate_has_content","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L118-L135","doc":"**The gate has falsifiable content: drop it and binding is no longer a function of the mutual\npart.** One fixed assembly — a single inter-component crossing and a single self-crossing, each of\nunit energy — read two ways: the self-crossing was already present in isolation\n(`isolatedMassTotal = 1`, the gate holds) or it was created by the assembly\n(`isolatedMassTotal = 0`, a type-I move, the gate fails). The mutual energy is `1` in both readings,\nand the two bindings differ. So `binding_indep_of_self` is a consequence of the gate, not of the\npartition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.binding_eq_neg_mutualEnergy_of_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.binding_eq_neg_mutualEnergy_of_gate","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L107-L116","doc":"**Recovering the landed result.** Under the gate, this file's binding agrees with\n`SelfMutualPartition.binding`, and both equal minus the mutual energy. Nothing is retracted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.binding_eq_neg_mutualEnergy_iff_selfDefect_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.binding_eq_neg_mutualEnergy_iff_selfDefect_zero","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L95-L105","doc":"**The gate, sharp.** Binding equals minus the mutual pairing **if and only if** the self\nreorganisation defect vanishes. This is the hypothesis the mass=self / binding=mutual assignment\nrests on, now visible in the type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.binding_eq_neg_mutual_add_selfDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.binding_eq_neg_mutual_add_selfDefect","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L84-L93","doc":"**The general mass-deficit identity.** Binding is minus the mutual energy *plus the self\nreorganisation defect*. `SelfMutualPartition.binding_eq_neg_mutualEnergy` is the `selfDefect = 0`\nslice of this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.selfDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.selfDefect","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L77-L82","doc":"**The self-crossing reorganisation defect** — the amount by which assembling the components\nchanges their own (intra-component) energy. Zero exactly when \"the self crossings are the ones\npresent in isolation\", the sentence `SelfMutualPartition` argues from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.bindingOfIsolated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.bindingOfIsolated","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SelfCrossingInvarianceGate.lean#L71-L75","doc":"**Binding by the mass deficit, with the isolated masses as free data.** `isolatedMassTotal` is\nthe sum of the component masses measured *in isolation*; nothing here presumes it equals the\nassembled diagram's self-crossing energy. ","signatureChunk":0}]}